Deferred call: amk_call_begin runs the handle's call in a fork of this parsed image and
hands back the pid and the read end of a pipe the result arrives on, so a guest's own
reactor can wait on it; amk_call_end reads the pipe, collects the child, applies the
writes it queued, and answers the text or the error the blocking call would have raised.
The child is a spawned job to the reaper and the sweep, through the slot setup the spawn
api now shares, and it closes every socket it inherited, so a server's connection closes
with its reply rather than with the call.

